1527	avalon_20251201_034434	proposal	100403	Alice	good	\N	From the mission results: M2 (Alice, Diana, Eve) failed, so at least one of Diana/Eve is evil; M3 (Bob, Charlie) failed, so at least one of Bob/Charlie is evil. As Alice, I know I’m good, so the two evils are among {Bob, Charlie, Diana, Eve}. Enumerating consistent combinations shows all of {Diana+Bob, Diana+Charlie, Eve+Bob, Eve+Charlie} are possible from results alone, so we need to lean on behavioral info.\n\nIn discussion, Charlie and Diana are strongly aligned, both heavily pushing the exact same trio (Alice+Charlie+Diana) and jointly steering suspicion toward Eve. That pairing is perfectly consistent with the evil set {Diana, Charlie}, where each caused the single fail on their respective missions and now want to sit together on the critical mission. Eve, by contrast, is the only one explicitly challenging the auto-clearing of Charlie and questioning that A+C should be locked in, which is a more town-leaning stance given Charlie’s presence on a failed mission.\n\nIf Diana and Charlie are the two evils, the only fully good trio including me is {Alice, Bob, Eve}. This team excludes both members of the Charlie–Diana bloc that are pushing hard to be together, avoids returning to the exact M3 fail pair, and uses the players whose positions are least mutually reinforcing from a potential coordinated-evil perspective.	[-0.015642393,0.022324493,-0.015270306,-0.018886907,0.03352065,0.058946397,0.007902036,-0.054908227,-0.011004249,0.044921964,-0.03683781,-0.05655228,0.055472482,-0.085096784,0.0022273487,0.04722389,-0.0028244876,0.016982421,-0.046423476,0.02870228,-0.084998764,-0.077363454,0.013131707,0.0143960165,-0.024919411,0.07608162,-0.021609835,-0.018621324,-0.01724786,-0.093296245,-0.005629743,0.07859814,0.06466335,0.0443352,0.004669869,0.028064841,-0.04958577,0.005635178,0.016309489,-0.0050839987,-0.029982828,0.0047377003,0.011172667,-0.06596714,-0.08615338,0.005916251,-0.019892784,0.03280262,0.030251773,