2075	avalon_20251201_055432	proposal	100401	Charlie	evil	\N	Given the information so far, the safest anchor we have is the Alice/Bob pair: they were together on Mission 3, which succeeded, and that team also aligns with the clean overlap from Mission 1 (Alice/Diana) versus the single-fail Mission 2 (Alice/Diana/Eve). The only structural difference between the clean M1/M3 core and the failed M2 is the addition of Eve, which strongly suggests the fail came from either Eve or, less likely, from some hidden complication in the overlap. By locking in Alice and Bob and adding me (Charlie), we avoid both of the main M2 suspects (Eve and, from some perspectives, Diana) while only introducing one new variable instead of revisiting the entire M2 minefield. If this team passes, we effectively confirm a strong good core for Mission 5; if it fails, we get very high-information feedback about the one new addition without reusing the suspicious configuration from Mission 2.	[-0.03454067,-0.039077353,0.0075796014,-0.06426635,0.093803674,-0.007660152,-0.014659099,-0.0080207875,-0.07415308,0.07471391,0.013327473,0.016312579,0.091513254,-0.12566376,-0.011328605,0.11610556,0.015716642,-0.00555081,-0.060383137,0.030012108,-0.073104344,-0.09168221,0.010902619,0.04727413,-0.07052005,0.029150866,-0.024626171,0.08642156,-0.039611045,-0.114840046,0.0148225,0.06812104,-0.00039131113,-0.009311089,0.051147398,0.03868724,-0.053301543,-0.02910038,0.009799629,-0.03994438,0.005348151,-0.037774246,0.05541782,-0.01798301,-0.008634265,0.038765304,0.012903453,0.01637603,-0.020678591,-0.005414173,-0.021192761,-0.026972836,0.0017357705,0.0014611975,-0.010197239,0.019663827,-0.048051428,0.0071259104,-0.03081477,0.030075416,0.044555094,0.03673053,-0.02870234,0.0035048898,0.08890232,-0.014040414,-0.055758014,-0.0144415945,0.0538589,0.066556275,0.06623751,-0.1023163,-0.052907437,-0.10310373,-0.05701094,0.16862611,0.026095755,0.016259607,0.036619768,-0.036310397,-0.0085887,-0.046543084,0.015831748,-0.01526444