1243	avalon_20251201_020734	proposal	100500	Bob	evil	\N	I’m keeping Alice and Diana because they were on both successful missions (AD and ADE), which strongly suggests they’re good. The main question is whether we trust Eve or me more for the third slot. The clean ADE result could easily have included a deep evil who chose to pass last round to look confirmed for this exact mission, since evil had strong incentive to appear safe going into 2–2. By contrast, if I were evil on ABD, I could have pushed for a repeat of that team or similar to close the game earlier rather than arguing against auto-locking ADE now. Given that AC also failed, Charlie is heavily implicated, so the most consistent world is that C is evil, and the second evil is either me or Eve. Between those, bringing back the ABD configuration with the two most consistently successful players (Alice and Diana) plus myself tests the more conservative, information-consistent hypothesis without auto-clearing Eve off a single convenient success.	[-0.06388279,-0.010719493,-0.03003493,-0.027325101,0.0074154465,0.034034792,0.011352731,-0.0128666395,-0.013452148,0.0569014,-0.04957238,0.012497353,0.0016474461,-0.069928594,0.015476283,0.04400781,0.031809494,-0.0343529,-0.06716365,0.033233773,-0.08290956,-0.077695206,-0.01838878,-0.029382206,-0.0140505405,0.030131496,0.0028945135,0.037482608,-0.051679384,-0.15090801,0.022480207,-0.0040117125,0.044001248,0.02122072,-0.019849742,-0.017684419,-0.047770787,-0.02905901,0.03152563,-0.0072194072,0.061697017,-0.01547033,-0.036486123,-0.050639518,-0.039946564,-0.021940678,-0.00916186,0.031166617,0.0190322,-0.044999946,0.013616727,-0.019820247,0.0073353834,-0.002811933,-0.05226391,0.06750615,0.034249954,0.018662782,-0.026623962,0.009430094,0.031647738,0.07804211,-0.056943882,0.024381435,0.03280809,0.021701995,-0.014876445,-0.033864927,-0.003670015,0.031765275,-0.020397719,-0.017877648,-0.11158358,-0.096878365,0.010598102,0.07987489,0.03023301,-0.06457402,0.07439464,-0.0628708