1240	avalon_20251201_020734	proposal	100400	Diana	good	\N	From my perspective, I know I’m good, and the two fails so far only tell me that the two evils are somewhere in {Alice, Bob, Charlie}. That makes Eve effectively confirmed good to me, since there are only two evils total. So Eve must be on this team. The last slot has to come from {Alice, Bob, Charlie}, where exactly one is good and two are evil. Purely from mission outcomes, Alice, Bob, and Charlie are symmetric candidates (each could be the lone good in one consistent pairing of two evils), so I have to lean on the discussion. Both Bob and Charlie are strongly aligned in pushing the “Alice is the common factor” narrative, which is exactly how a Bob–Charlie evil pair would try to frame things if Alice were actually good. Eve, who I view as good, is more wary of Charlie than Alice after the 2‑person fail and explicitly prefers including Alice while warning against putting Bob and Charlie together. That lines up with the theory that Bob and Charlie are the evil pair and Alice is good. Given all that, the most consistent good team I can form is Alice, me, and Eve.	[0.016679248,-0.013657772,-0.02408651,-0.050805453,-0.0141817825,0.0503997,-0.024893237,-0.038079586,0.020466242,0.020991355,-0.090091534,-0.013623435,0.054455448,-0.022181591,0.009205985,0.04139062,0.024373507,0.03562794,0.0041447575,0.0493813,-0.093243964,-0.121834725,-0.004861813,-0.076791406,-0.044728708,0.042274434,-0.0048399665,-0.060403258,-0.031114496,-0.10579029,-0.024095293,0.031076917,0.03266815,0.030209498,-0.029544525,0.02653128,0.0026508807,-0.008345485,0.0424375,0.008373661,-0.0009722024,-0.011025449,-0.026037643,-0.058396205,-0.09946979,0.016906878,0.043460548,0.052008204,-0.0024113988,-0.084127925,-0.046892133,0.0013643091,-0.008161047,0.015461991,0.063826695,0.047806386,-0.0029404557,-0.020246277,-0.030086681,-0.009683661,0.02234313,0.05528374,-0.066515304,0.020690493,0.08798241,0.014882005,-0.03945337,0.07753128,-0.09824872,0.071809