1350	avalon_20251201_024547	proposal	100500	Diana	good	\N	Given the board state, I’m sticking with the logic I laid out earlier: I don’t want a team that can naturally contain both suspected evils from the structural pairs we’ve been debating. The two natural suspicion pairs from the mission outcomes are {Alice, Eve} off the M2 fail and {Charlie, Diana} off the M4 fail, with Bob sitting in the middle as the common element on both failed missions. If we pick from those pairs in a way that allows both evils to land together (like {Alice, Charlie, Diana} or {Bob, Alice, Charlie}), we risk a double-evil team in a must-succeed spot. By choosing {Alice, Bob, Diana}, we’re taking one player who was on the M2 fail (Alice), one who was on both fails (Bob), and one from the M3 clean pair (Diana), but critically we’re *not* taking both members of either suspicion pair together. This keeps us away from obviously high-risk double-evil constructions while still using players who have been on successful missions (Alice on M1, Bob and Diana on M3) and avoids the very contentious Charlie/Eve slot entirely on the final mission.	[0.018558089,0.010538571,0.01898778,-0.065114014,0.056619853,0.027202757,0.006371667,0.0066548805,0.03768713,0.045152362,-0.05744351,0.018152427,0.086183764,0.011604348,0.011485501,0.074208476,0.014117691,0.03992781,-0.0013237331,0.09035923,-0.06729704,-0.120578684,-0.03185196,-0.038382515,-0.06256135,0.028328422,0.019484147,0.034534186,-0.015700778,-0.10473997,0.056774072,0.05969225,-0.002574405,0.008311036,0.016409485,0.014521783,-0.023821125,-0.019900292,0.029588735,-0.039377764,0.0023348203,-0.0018443313,0.016176019,-0.044540346,-0.08442528,0.021969877,0.034866102,0.038143553,0.023755414,-0.05497596,0.004839336,-0.021390516,0.012371516,0.032674752,0.008108944,0.029175509,-0.06237129,-0.0026770015,-0.039412573,0.025869869,0.022651507,0.02710116,-0.04608592,-0.020265698,0.06665629,0.05048771,-0.010491939,0.041987196,-0.049353726,0.115282066,0.027933335,-0.04