1414	avalon_20251201_030844	proposal	100400	Bob	good	\N	From the mission results we can publicly deduce Bob is good: if Bob were evil, the fail on Mission 3 (team [Charlie, Diana]) would be impossible, since neither Charlie nor Diana could then be evil enough to account for all fails. Mission 2 (Alice, Bob, Eve) had exactly one fail, so with Bob good, it means exactly one of {Alice, Eve} is evil. Mission 3 (Charlie, Diana) had exactly one fail, so exactly one of {Charlie, Diana} is evil. So the two evils are one from {Alice, Eve} and one from {Charlie, Diana}. Looking at the discussion, Charlie behaves inconsistently with a good player: if he were good, knowing he himself is good, he should conclude Diana is the only candidate evil in {Charlie, Diana} and avoid putting her on teams, yet he repeatedly suggests including Diana. That strongly points to Charlie as the evil from that pair, making Diana good. Eve’s push for the exact double-suspect pairing (Eve, Bob, Charlie) conveniently includes both likely evils (herself and Charlie), which fits her as the other evil rather than Alice. That leaves the good team as {Alice, Bob, Diana}, which I’m proposing here.	[-0.022326931,-0.00023701823,-0.007922797,-0.049514845,-0.00056010246,0.025313327,0.0069359536,-0.02074691,-0.002008849,0.05330249,-0.057005107,-0.023910867,0.07506409,-0.064616695,0.019169614,0.03268838,0.013214718,0.055509627,-0.032160044,0.037894443,-0.06104382,-0.0773177,-0.004864294,-0.010199057,-0.051535636,0.06221129,-0.008333264,-0.025431167,-0.034289423,-0.091946535,-0.018037999,0.05407055,0.037814118,0.0671565,0.019311866,0.010787348,-0.018079454,0.00020736452,-0.032078955,0.015052109,-0.0016562094,-0.029373284,-0.049724404,-0.061615568,-0.093296185,-0.015343235,0.020211015,0.024939211,0.042782865,-0.08509603,-0.032791395,0.0019764453,-0.016612884,-0.007889545,0.013585309,0.02928823,-0.032850146,0.021008195,-0.021703316,0.024234181,0.0033205692,0.05475556,-0.050377786,-0.002431377,0.111599684,0.00591824