1585	avalon_20251201_040534	proposal	100401	Bob	good	\N	I know Eve is evil from Mission 3 (I played success and there was exactly one fail), so she must be one of the two evil players. The other evil is in {Diana, Alice, Charlie} from the single-fail Mission 2. Eve is strongly pushing to exclude Diana and to form a team of Bob/Alice/Charlie, which only helps her if her unseen partner is in {Alice, Charlie}. That makes Diana more likely to be good. Both Alice and Diana are proposing structures that avoid Eve and acknowledge the split evil in {Alice, Charlie} and {Bob, Eve}, which matches the actual constraint from my perspective. To minimize the chance of including the second evil, I lock in myself and the most likely good (Diana) and then choose the player who isn’t being hard-pushed by the known evil, which is Alice over Charlie. So Bob–Alice–Diana avoids Eve entirely and avoids the exact trio the known evil player is lobbying for.	[0.022760702,0.027011853,-0.009819152,-0.05291625,0.004388761,0.028514005,0.013894387,-0.01078444,0.015150205,0.04744352,-0.045001905,-0.03592297,0.045311257,-0.05645423,0.020864377,0.044644307,0.043490335,0.056319065,-0.017084323,0.041255113,-0.052074704,-0.112545975,0.0028627517,-0.029715851,-0.03222638,0.021958476,-0.0022208197,0.00022857184,-0.0047454285,-0.12578902,0.023253834,0.00635898,0.045793056,0.043586377,-0.0429649,0.0061987876,-0.058098476,-0.028018044,-0.028733203,-0.0073869117,-0.026948374,0.013418585,-0.047093727,-0.07590691,-0.09305381,-0.012106596,-0.009483104,0.07104234,0.052058812,-0.10069631,-0.019625258,0.001695739,-0.05648556,0.0433706,0.033285722,0.026391102,-0.036735214,0.0199275,-0.060278937,0.039125934,0.058831494,0.05197583,-0.030478379,0.0007874581,0.09818923,0.014865263,-0.017899511,0.033948317,-0.10337636,0.06816585,0.029745504,-0.04887668,-0.11463338,-0.07788177,0.013625781,0.021877673,0.1139649,-0.038186196,0.049029157,0.0074511617,-0.014528085,-0.04272669,0.0017420391,0.12533441,0.042182703,-0.03468453,-