1735	avalon_20251201_043844	proposal	100401	Alice	good	\N	Given the mission history, this is the tightest, most self-consistent good block we can form. Mission 1 (Charlie + Diana) was clean, so that pair is at least capable of passing a mission together. Mission 3 (Diana + Alice) was a clean 2-person mission, which is a very strong signal that both Diana and Alice are good or, at minimum, that there was no incentive to fail there. The single fail on Mission 2 came from among {Bob, Charlie, Alice}; but with Alice and Diana passing together on M3 and Charlie and Diana passing together on M1, the combination that best explains all three results without stretching is that the fail came from Bob. That makes Bob the first exclusion, and since the remaining evil would then most likely be off the clean pairings (i.e., more consistent with Eve than with the Alice–Charlie–Diana triangle), the safest and most data-backed team is Alice + Charlie + Diana. This team maximizes overlap with proven clean configurations while excluding the highest-probability source of the prior fail.	[-0.073432945,0.0026644778,-0.032867014,-0.0521725,-0.014346174,-0.0073935073,-0.058159325,-0.017851746,0.0002579255,0.046528928,-0.037701916,0.0097544445,0.09127939,-0.09105414,0.017636085,0.061022405,0.01199973,0.023844413,-0.031541456,0.00806798,-0.11986286,-0.06756291,-0.015002188,0.046339467,-0.015497061,0.0970675,-0.027768167,-0.047191128,-0.013309965,-0.1332703,-0.0063371663,0.004101672,0.03060176,0.031804804,0.004058561,0.02947388,-0.016411923,-0.0009996193,-0.008152783,0.0078051183,-0.029632436,-0.006476935,-0.01877861,-0.050154094,-0.06650173,-0.023826215,0.012902001,0.017824106,0.024327502,-0.060465306,-0.018390007,-0.0012686831,-0.0046026814,0.061954875,0.04674937,-0.022618733,-0.052968394,0.010347558,-0.04214061,0.022638852,0.0066057467,0.05653924,-0.06174038,-0.0015065147,0.111039124,0.025613725,-0.02946247,-0.003183225,0.0040517137,0.064014696,0.0042449953,-0.060952716,-0.10648072,-0.0494