1780	avalon_20251201_044722	proposal	100402	Charlie	good	\N	We have two failed missions to work from. Mission 2 (Diana, Alice, Eve) and Mission 3 (Bob, Charlie) each had exactly one fail, so each of Alice and Bob has now been on a different failing team. That makes both Alice and Bob highly suspect, and putting either of them back on a critical Mission 4 team is a big risk when we’re already at 1–2. The only trio that completely avoids both previously failing overlaps (Alice from M2 and Bob from M3) is Charlie, Diana, and Eve. While Diana/Eve appeared together on the failed M2 team, that team also included Alice, so the blame can’t be cleanly assigned to either of them individually. In contrast, Bob was on the only other fail, and Alice was the unique addition on the M2 fail. Given the limited information and the need to minimize exposure to the highest-risk players, the safest, most consistent choice is to exclude both Alice and Bob and run with Charlie, Diana, and Eve.	[-0.01943952,0.010177411,0.006978783,-0.06294818,0.09456456,0.047762536,-0.019224346,-0.014578127,-0.0017952853,0.02880572,0.017483965,0.006935466,0.091080084,-0.0357643,0.0049380176,0.010326,-0.030157465,0.03177285,-0.02801365,-0.042538226,-0.060915723,-0.102703504,-0.04996971,0.0749413,-0.06851426,0.042804535,-0.018287146,0.05456867,-0.062148076,-0.084367625,0.00839674,-0.014427559,0.024121562,-0.0075225895,0.010501232,0.033362556,-0.061057538,0.012806108,0.021669354,-0.030981952,0.004689868,0.007662437,-0.006906263,-0.02867679,-0.06635035,-0.016671713,0.018165857,0.03330362,0.015988108,-0.007606878,0.0112729035,-0.034636706,-0.03044788,0.046125673,0.035896923,-0.0059311404,-0.060769055,-0.0051740394,-0.037798785,0.016034512,-0.029981613,0.037526187,-0.044860758,0.016191918,0.08669993,0.060040474,-0.046702094,0.018727882,-0.020364929,0.119738646,0.043793194,-0.039092626,-0.05451969,-0.058474377,-0.036551107,0.12721284,0.03991719,-0.01507008,-0.00051168544,-0.036968082,-0.01179388,-0.059950117,-0.0