1980	avalon_20251201_052452	proposal	100501	Alice	good	\N	Given the mission history, the only player who has been on every *successful* mission is Alice, and Charlie has only ever appeared on clean missions as well. The core {Alice, Charlie} has never produced a fail. We then need to decide between re‑including Bob or pulling in someone from {Diana, Eve}, both of whom are tied to at least one failed mission. While Bob was on both fails, each of those teams also included at least one of {Charlie, Diana, Eve}, so we can’t cleanly isolate him as the unique problem without also assuming very specific double‑good/double‑evil patterns that don’t line up neatly with the clean missions. If we avoid Bob, we’re forced to bring in either Diana or Eve, who each only have evidence from the failed runs. By contrast, the trio Alice–Bob–Charlie is the only 3‑person combination that (1) fully contains the repeatedly clean Alice–Charlie core, (2) has a concrete clean data point involving Alice–Bob, and (3) stays entirely away from both Diana and Eve, who are only associated with failures. On balance, Alice–Bob–Charlie is the most consistent team with the success/fail pattern while minimizing exposure to players only seen on failed missions.	[-0.024844225,0.00044812428,0.022292122,-0.07984197,-0.012457975,0.009054688,0.010554515,-0.044772048,0.01632923,0.046134163,-0.058260027,-0.030929225,0.072832346,-0.053690482,0.013531475,0.057010688,-0.006435794,0.069538504,-0.011435519,-0.016492598,-0.08183208,-0.07539659,-0.03865794,0.020285616,-0.048880227,0.06676962,-0.010789373,-0.019112961,-0.02203366,-0.117631756,0.022020668,0.03740122,0.057915077,0.03107363,0.017059866,0.09297669,-0.08398309,-0.012745032,3.420434e-05,-0.009144026,0.006654321,-0.027627248,-0.01609584,-0.065933526,-0.06340102,-0.030177018,-0.019862838,0.037191715,0.011882258,-0.04082485,-0.011379268,-0.007465947,-0.005378412,0.062367477,0.07899814,-0.032904524,-0.007800631,-0.05379909,-0.054022398,-0.0064344453,0.0071883094