2011	avalon_20251201_053824	proposal	100500	Bob	good	\N	I know I’m good, and the two failed missions (2 and 4) each had exactly one fail. That means one spy must be in {Charlie, Diana} and the other in {Alice, Eve}, but it can’t be the same person on both missions. The table talk then matters a lot. Alice and Charlie are both very eager to anchor on the M3 pair (Alice+Eve) and frame me as the common denominator, even though from a good perspective Alice should be at least somewhat suspicious of Eve after the M4 fail (since only Bob or Eve could have failed that mission from her seat). That overconfidence in the Alice–Eve pair makes Alice more suspicious than Eve. Between Charlie and Diana, Diana’s reasoning about benching an entire suspect pair and building a {Bob, Diana, Eve} team matches the logical structure I see as good and is the only suggestion that doesn’t double down on the “Bob is the problem” narrative. The most consistent world with both the mission results and the discussion has spies as {Charlie, Alice}, making {Bob, Diana, Eve} the all-good trio. Even in other plausible worlds, this team is at least as safe as any alternative that includes me, and it aligns with the only argument that doesn’t rely on tunneling me as the common denominator.	[0.009769457,-0.007987975,-0.028174201,-0.053238377,0.05846207,-0.0017087623,0.036116507,-0.015767984,0.011119741,0.08648933,-0.040079635,0.0131004425,0.12377631,-0.040389873,0.017406788,0.06852912,0.029090572,-0.0031893482,-0.059375297,0.040555112,-0.08098256,-0.1209044,0.084641196,-0.0049419184,-0.07325006,0.05883036,-0.010086332,-0.045051478,-0.044307258,-0.076976605,0.042799905,0.069416314,0.013506154,0.016243795,0.028442254,0.027460873,0.007991064,-0.033010177,0.06392966,-0.00052834407,0.00648218,-0.04263086,0.012210953,-0.04817002,-0.07163137,0.028554186,0.036329843,0.03913264,0.013043679,-0.05586348,-0.052390665,-0.011263567,-0.040932458,-0.010033844,0.014231365,0.009687272,-0.051581338,0.020613568,-0.0010885