2076	avalon_20251201_055432	proposal	100500	Diana	good	\N	Given I know I’m good, I want to anchor the team on myself and avoid the most suspicious overlaps. Both mission fails can be explained in many ways, but the strongest structural suspicion falls on Alice: she appears on both failed missions (M2 with Diana/Eve and M4 with Bob/Charlie) and is also the common factor across all missions. Additionally, both Alice and Bob are pushing hard to keep the Alice–Bob pair intact on the decisive mission, which is exactly what an evil player in that pair would want after two clean results. To reduce the risk of handing the game to a possibly compromised pair, I’m excluding Alice and choosing Bob plus Charlie: Bob has a clean result with Alice on M3 and was already on the M4 fail (meaning if he’s evil, we’re likely doomed no matter what we pick), while Charlie’s only appearance was on M4, where he could be framed by an already-suspicious Alice. The trio Bob–Charlie–Diana avoids Alice and Eve (the latter only ever appeared on the failed M2) and is the most consistent way, from my perspective, to minimize exposure to the most suspect overlaps on the final mission.	[-0.011391423,0.010984509,0.0022429705,-0.06327629,0.08715571,0.020534633,0.031378094,-0.022420166,0.012735691,0.028587585,0.0040643555,0.011862276,0.10167497,-0.056787703,-0.011153501,0.05113063,0.037643276,0.040603284,-0.029214503,0.018580653,-0.08473383,-0.15478837,-0.0011293434,-0.023218894,-0.051929034,0.022102254,0.013424882,-0.0032383415,-0.018030073,-0.11577315,0.029992176,0.011226191,0.014984126,-0.010116986,-0.009924662,0.004999596,-0.057326548,0.014753659,0.037998263,-0.031202901,0.0071945884,-0.0073315413,0.017500423,-0.07187783,-0.08015872,-0.0045282356,0.023851765,0.063580036,0.04525266,-0.07698337,0.00220365,-0.03320136,-0.021033198,0.029289173,0.026173156,-0.0017836047,-0.052962217,0.0132670645,-0.061143856,0.03668318,-0.003336487,0.056708496,-0.040259466,-0.0052325125,0.06713217,0.055576738,-0.0284511