960	avalon_20251201_001747	proposal	100401	Eve	evil	\N	I don’t like hard-locking Alice+Diana as a guaranteed good core off two 2‑person successes, since an evil on those teams could easily choose to pass both to earn exactly that trust. Re-running both of them together now effectively bets the game on that assumption. By choosing [Alice, Charlie, Eve], we (1) still keep Alice, who has been on all successful missions, (2) include Charlie, who’s generally trusted and avoids the prior failing configuration with Bob, and (3) bring in me as the only fully untested player to actually challenge the current narrative instead of just looping the same pair. This team avoids Bob, who is currently the most directly associated with the only fail, while also not auto-confirming Diana by default, giving the table more meaningful information than just repeating the Alice–Diana combo.	[-0.039996892,-0.027847722,-0.035191923,-0.03307382,-0.012652493,0.046221763,0.0485018,-0.006545685,-0.02365066,0.07550707,-0.04169418,-0.011825518,0.06719464,-0.05680892,-0.0024012926,0.08466658,0.013795637,0.018918596,-0.00993988,0.03123328,-0.094576515,-0.12301485,0.00095520366,0.017432902,0.022177834,0.0133528225,-0.022484975,0.041631874,-0.03947252,-0.10675759,-0.043906752,0.007478078,-0.009621372,0.02882425,-0.01959986,-0.009845796,-0.06890539,0.0328611,0.0126433,-0.050399806,-0.006530724,-0.11212913,0.0007756856,-0.07505265,-0.08362258,0.008490197,0.01642417,0.08487677,-0.019427244,-0.026711173,-0.025241038,0.03195964,0.022707041,-0.036684066,0.038200583,0.0613588,0.017234726,0.03301417,-0.019223869,0.023070393,-0.010508347,0.0592024,-0.0628733,0.042029288,0.05019416,0.024868047,-0.017299715,0.017787542,-0.0010240405,0.08243595,0.0560127,-0.036812022,-0.09540922,-0.09369492,-0.016164228,0.047335993,0.025017982,-0.09563652,0.023198983,0.025350822,-0.029663783,-0.046060756,0.011859827,0.07947297,0.01914634,-0.029400548,-0.0025182976,-0.05451063,0.07116728,-0.056252502,0.0035138314,-0.056934852,0.1