1154	avalon_20251201_013236	proposal	100500	Bob	good	\N	Both failed missions had exactly one FAIL, and each was created by adding Alice to a previously clean-looking core: Mission 2 added Alice to the Charlie/Diana pair and failed, and Mission 4 added Alice to the Bob/Eve pair and failed. Since Alice was the new addition on both single-fail teams but is widely townread and consistently included in everyone’s proposals, the more consistent explanation is that the evils are among the overlapping pairs around her, not Alice herself. Mission 1’s Charlie+Diana and Mission 3’s Bob+Eve both passed as 2-person teams; introducing Alice then produced single fails when combined with (Charlie,Diana) and (Bob,Eve) respectively. To avoid repeating either suspicious pair, we should keep Diana and Eve off together and combine the most trusted from each side: Charlie rather than Diana from {Charlie, Diana}, and Bob rather than Eve from {Bob, Eve}, plus Alice as the common trusted anchor. This gives us the only all-new 3-person combo that avoids every previously suspicious pairing: Alice, Bob, and Charlie.	[-0.008496876,-0.02679659,-0.007756555,-0.034049936,0.008315399,-0.0048869946,-0.039917342,-0.059714884,0.0023323384,0.03234099,-0.010532997,-0.042911354,0.068707235,-0.07966074,0.04778883,0.05625717,-0.027339265,0.05189518,-0.00031023752,0.019161534,-0.09673568,-0.08817573,-0.017400865,0.036113504,-0.03439903,0.049222313,-0.046327293,-0.027664699,-0.029841112,-0.09804701,0.012392502,0.06336827,0.02743419,0.035075605,0.045594137,0.02316343,-0.0067947027,0.03936902,0.028826809,-0.008250669,-0.007776793,-0.016585438,0.0065438827,-0.054227613,-0.10812933,-0.011161579,0.006800312,0.0020652444,0.059619643,-0.081129834,0.026720753,-0.00019787453,-0.027197191,0.018901652,0.011133642,0.018539406,-0.068491675,0.064150125,-0.036759846,0.025891388,-0.0068835737,0.08791778,-0.043417543,-0.0011083428,0.07830102,0.024622262,-0.059745055,-0.040875513,-0.03489568,0.07646481,0.046531204,-0.06083091