1124	avalon_20251201_012415	proposal	100400	Bob	good	\N	We know Mission 2 (Bob, Diana, Eve) and Mission 3 (Alice, Charlie) each had exactly one fail, so there is at least one evil in {Diana, Eve} and at least one evil in {Alice, Charlie}. As Bob, I know I’m good, so the evil on Mission 2 must be in {Diana, Eve}, and we still have one evil in {Alice, Charlie}. Eve’s reasoning in discussion was logically off in a way that conveniently clears herself while blaming me, which I know is false, making her significantly more likely to be evil than Diana. Charlie has been strongly pushing to keep a Bob–Charlie core and repeatedly include Eve, which looks like potential partner-cover if Eve is evil, and also steers away from Alice and Diana together—exactly the pair I now most want to test. If the evil pair is Charlie–Eve, then Bob–Alice–Diana is all good and can succeed; if instead one of Alice/Diana is actually evil, we still only have one evil on the team, and they must choose between outing themselves with a fail on the decisive mission or passing and risking a good victory on Quest 5. Among all viable options, Bob–Alice–Diana both best matches behavioral reads (Eve and Charlie most suspicious) and avoids repeating either exact failing combo while not giving obvious comfort to any suspected pairing.	[-0.0043814927,0.02330819,-0.010676414,-0.02105447,0.009295031,0.04290065,0.008287453,-0.05136363,0.0011778479,0.061936937,-0.099085666,-0.023094425,0.045887515,-0.03354238,0.0121477265,0.053404603,0.012392255,0.06258179,-0.041165445,0.05203855,-0.06614099,-0.076421544,-0.011171661,-0.023671193,-0.062426325,0.019559251,-0.015842851,-0.05100369,-0.05584664,-0.10843456,0.002306504,0.04750897,-0.026924875,0.032468263,0.004714809,0.007538853,-0.02286878,0.026381597,0.01549099,-0.0069627455,-0.011842333,-0.02336206,-0.04174519,-0.07078253,-0.07982008,-0.0060476284,-0.018307442,0.03676874,0.059907246,-0.09426065,-0.018899703,-0.017898912,-0.05249603,0.0003688892,-0.00080053945,0.020