1449	avalon_20251201_031607	proposal	100502	Bob	good	\N	Given the mission outcomes and the final-round arguments, the configurations that best fit both the card results and the social behavior most often have Diana as evil from Mission 2 and one of Charlie/Eve as the partner. The way both Charlie and Diana converged on pushing a Bob–Charlie–Eve team—while heavily insisting Alice sit out after being on both fails—looks like coordinated pressure away from Alice, who is actually more likely good but now an easy scapegoat. Eve’s insistence on the Alice–Bob–Eve team and her skepticism of Charlie’s early leadership read more like a good player trying (perhaps clumsily) to keep what she believes is a clean core together than like an evil player overreaching. Under the most consistent reading, the all-good trio is Alice–Bob–Eve, so that is the team I propose.	[-0.028141944,-0.004901158,-0.051641222,-0.046017703,-0.051298626,0.06708684,-0.03009887,-0.022838218,-0.009357346,0.039867327,-0.052019518,0.01127166,0.043157604,-0.06643403,0.027020134,0.043141566,0.045468334,0.033225294,0.024614483,0.062437594,-0.087488234,-0.10127846,0.021932364,0.00970257,-0.06538831,0.05890383,0.007718889,-0.048058115,-0.03949689,-0.10994471,-0.01066213,0.025034223,0.0460965,0.058494516,-0.034343068,0.042467643,0.0020242874,0.015124469,-0.017933663,0.0017352273,0.011216201,-0.042059045,-0.022288661,-0.080824405,-0.063476376,-0.0087130135,0.036328003,0.015173961,0.0058990875,-0.07740133,-0.017203998,-0.04795655,-0.01026453,-0.008468877,0.022670284,0.030284904,0.0054800767,-0.012649744,0.0013938774,0.01783964,0.023050185,0.07677584,-0.031380996,0.024665965,0.059247453,0.019483976,-0.04575054,0.07654196,-0.07378836,0.05252531,0.042595413,-0.05928116,-0.044685826,-0.12182316,-0.038783383,0.066692635,0.0817524,-0.08417571,0.061863165,0.0054866215,-0.018916523,-0.04730008,0.0031601014,0.1325146,0.011402499,-0.04337869,-0.058716588,-0.07306128,0.067851186,0.04576132,-0.08558039,0.032472104,0.09951439,0.