1241	avalon_20251201_020734	proposal	100401	Eve	good	\N	We have two consistent worlds with the mission history: (1) Alice is evil plus one of {Bob, Charlie}, or (2) Alice is good and both Bob and Charlie are evil. In world (1), evil is comfortable with Alice staying on teams; in world (2), evil needs Alice off future teams and will loudly frame her as the common denominator. Notice that after Mission 3, both Bob and Charlie immediately pushed to bench Alice and keep a Bob/Charlie core in contention, which lines up much more naturally with world (2) than with Alice as the single common evil. The two‑person fail of Alice+Charlie can be explained by Charlie being the single evil there just as easily as by Alice, and the Alice+Bob+Diana fail doesn’t implicate Diana specifically over Bob. Given that, the safest construction that breaks the Bob/Charlie axis while still using prior mission info is to lock in Alice and Diana (who were on the mixed 3‑person team) and add me as the fresh third. This gives us a team with no Bob/Charlie, the pair most incentivized to misdirect after the last fail, and maximizes the chance of a clean mission without giving in to what could be coordinated framing of Alice.	[-0.027434072,-0.005156415,-0.024253989,-0.046987716,0.015768774,-0.008824821,-0.053054865,-0.028349634,0.051084314,0.056229964,0.0022860046,-0.037049275,0.04775277,-0.016614225,0.027089441,0.015396183,0.009463139,0.03051749,-0.07412498,0.015427048,-0.07303434,-0.06495817,0.006500129,0.035871394,-0.047725055,0.018718874,-0.015138174,0.037306283,0.020126969,-0.080606066,-0.026865222,0.050888117,0.03708485,0.022733407,-0.02964822,0.033228565,-0.069061756,0.03784266,0.02286355,0.0016229093,-0.02949147,0.013855813,-0.026090093,-0.0722145,-0.101978995,0.008332427,0.009346493,0.020208525,0.020976104,-0.042615492,-0.016213564,0.00954843,0.0022160616,0.020184811,0.04472987,0.029181767,0.0061012697,0.06233237,-0.04565262,0.009273699,-0.029476589,0.009109972,-0.032724738,-0.017220784,0.0