1352	avalon_20251201_024547	proposal	100502	Alice	good	\N	From my perspective as Alice (known good to myself), the only impossible evil pairs given the mission results are {Alice, Eve} (would make Mission 4 impossible to fail) and {Charlie, Diana} (would make Mission 2 impossible to fail with only 1 FAIL). Eliminating myself from consideration, the remaining structurally possible evil pairs are {Bob, Charlie}, {Bob, Diana}, {Bob, Eve}, {Charlie, Eve}, and {Diana, Eve}. This means that Charlie and Diana cannot both be evil together. Any team I pick of the form {Alice, X, Y} that includes a pair which can be jointly evil risks a double-evil team; the only pair among {Bob, Charlie, Diana, Eve} that is guaranteed NOT to be double-evil is {Charlie, Diana}. Therefore, {Alice, Charlie, Diana} is the unique team that structurally cannot contain two evil players. While it’s still possible that exactly one of Charlie or Diana is evil, this team strictly minimizes the worst-case risk (no double-evil scenario), which is the best we can do with the available information.	[-0.0010078716,0.041933212,-0.037132,-0.055910703,-0.010663793,0.039449416,-0.034562327,-0.038780425,0.022141404,0.01860195,-0.052963253,0.016216034,0.07086656,0.026863111,-0.0010941783,0.04424972,-0.0022643898,0.07428956,-0.020010566,0.022932338,-0.03733517,-0.13107209,-0.053143732,0.0120421825,-0.038601425,0.048495643,-0.004076128,0.00045121292,-0.05246841,-0.13099712,-0.0033009406,0.015630087,0.017871844,0.0570969,0.011638222,0.0072714775,-0.051044792,0.02350089,0.026505545,-0.007721859,-0.045429375,-0.00013829705,-0.021982409,-0.06310826,-0.07784021,0.0021885575,0.013714021,0.006536471,0.0521898,-0.050033245,-0.022600604,-0.013332425,-0.019166969,0.019284096,0.07038238,-0.0017475813,-0.099912986,-0.02026004,-0.058357857,0.039489772,0.040337265,0.047830552,-0.028790962,-0.00893623,0.06668917,0.027848521,-0.018830203,0.066165715,-0.09302905,0.068484046,0.053740513,-0.045768842,-0.056360282,-0.08367311,-0.02169