1448	avalon_20251201_031607	proposal	100501	Alice	good	\N	From mission results, at least one of {Bob, Diana} must be evil (mission 2 fail) and at least one of {Charlie, Eve} must be evil (mission 4 fail). They cannot both evils be in the same pair, or we couldn’t explain both fails, so the evil team is one from each pair. As Alice, I know I’m good. That means any team including me plus exactly one from each pair is doomed to contain both evils—unless we correctly identify which from each pair is actually good. Behaviorally: Diana led both failing missions (2 and 4) and was on the first fail, which makes her the most suspicious in {Bob, Diana}. Eve was leader on the clean 2-player mission (3) with me and has consistently argued for a team that includes me, which aligns with me knowing I’m good and makes her more likely good than Charlie in {Charlie, Eve}. The most coherent good-world is therefore: Bob good, Eve good, Diana and Charlie evil. Under that configuration, the only all-good team we can form is Alice–Bob–Eve, so that’s the team I propose.	[0.0026124401,-0.0014134301,-0.005394665,-0.06406677,0.0034178183,0.0068489322,0.007656196,-0.06671443,-0.002572163,0.032705214,-0.06383902,-0.03649472,0.09579746,-0.044992846,0.010683825,0.033479672,0.02089793,0.03788979,-0.044659972,0.030979015,-0.071661666,-0.096965246,-0.0067441976,-0.008218361,-0.071880646,0.04704742,-0.017292568,-0.04764626,-0.03644885,-0.11442925,-0.03968797,0.042259928,0.035560668,0.059547186,0.0038337926,0.039118305,-0.04239974,0.020807918,0.02061153,-0.012936627,-0.0063229096,-0.018944968,-0.029002145,-0.043273088,-0.1276454,0.015304766,0.0256833,0.030298354,0.03058236,-0.0712598,-0.026964935,0.0036152161,-0.008626811,0.018436495,0.05927156,0.03621596,-0.030448865,-0.0041085626,-0.016764326,-0.014153925,0.016668424,0.045771983,-0.028837914,-0.00046838375,0.071543135,0.02708785,-0.04704174,0.09779487,-0.10678672,0.041749075,0.03947391,-0.05438809,-0.053047843,-0.055620063,-0.051852677,0.078474686,0