1347	avalon_20251201_024547	proposal	100300	Alice	good	\N	Mission 2 (Alice, Bob, Eve) produced a single fail, so we know at least one of those three is evil and possibly more. For a 2-person Mission 3, the safest approach is to avoid that entire contaminated set and use the only fresh pair that hasn’t touched a failed team: Charlie and Diana. Mission 1’s success with Alice and Eve doesn’t clear either of them, since a single good-leaning success is easy for evil to allow through early. By sending Charlie and Diana, we maximize distance from the known bad information while still using a pairing all three of Bob, Charlie, and Eve independently called the cleanest structural test. This gives us the highest chance of a pure team right now and the clearest info going into Mission 4.	[-0.028323194,0.02170156,-0.009332423,-0.053269308,0.030732654,-0.047203183,-0.041692365,-0.015297185,-0.010099361,0.058801416,-0.03521341,0.02719411,0.05554811,-0.057512987,-0.01799565,0.0033953977,0.02177018,0.010600312,-0.010073279,0.020797547,-0.08577157,-0.0732835,-0.00656898,0.033714514,-0.015972227,0.068956204,-0.035843063,-0.04666158,-0.044321734,-0.113742895,0.019707091,0.058551993,0.046337202,-0.000837027,0.04858175,0.043243933,0.037588213,-0.02861518,0.019238085,-0.01157297,0.0039257156,-0.0351968,-0.019107256,-0.0057271863,-0.044856805,0.012305689,0.02661423,0.003590735,0.05186852,-0.055964235,5.145858e-05,-0.04724908,0.008681859,0.022794327,0.034126807,-0.013960443,-0.06278618,-0.014749692,-0.059412364,0.049511556,0.0451813,0.044882733,-0.05310994,-0.003660239,0.09013201,0.058434606,-0.0063006887,-0.007411627,0.029906768,0.046106856,0.019978138,-0.042142887,-0.0632711,-0.0712301,-0.037422314,0.11718274,0.061116386,-0.054590967,0.009448274,-0.025325473,-0.026084373,-0.12410966,0.022433808,0.09799378,-0.015724344,0.005194892,-0.035542138,-0.049411096,0.04923084,0.019486401,-0.035346583,0.03226394,0.11496944,0.06261155,0.08001133,0.10825019,-0.009698364,-0.013781846,0.026508301,0.10